# Atom framework state
#
# events.jsonl is a machine-generated append-only log -- genuinely not source.
#
# .atom/state.json is deliberately NOT ignored (B173). It records project
# configuration and human approvals, which are project history. Ignoring it is
# what made `atom status` report "Phase: unknown" in this very repository: the
# file Atom treated as its sole source of truth never survived a clone. What is
# left in it now cannot be derived from the filesystem, so it has to be kept.
.atom/events.jsonl

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

